{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id34985699"}, "name":{"label":"gatorfantom"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2013-09-05T21:30:38-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"3"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.2.0"}, "id":{"label":"866139514"}, "title":{"label":"I enjoy F@W, but this app seems redundant"}, "content":{"label":"As an early beta tester I've been using the F@W online music player since the beginning. I was excited when the iOS app launched, but after trying it out for a while I'm not really sure why it even exists. What I mean by that is: A) the majority of links / buttons within the app simply launch the mobile Safari app and load a page from the F@W website (which actually gets pretty annoying after the first 3-4 times); and B) the app doesn't seem to offer anything that isn't already available on said site. \n\nWhereas, if I use F@W on mobile Safari instead of the app, at least it won't keep opening up another application.\n\nSo I guess my question is: what's the purpose of this app? What do users gain by installing another 10MB app vs simply using the mobile website?", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=638810714&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
